WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:05.940
So aluminium is a metal which was only isolated
in the 19th

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.270
century and when it was first isolated it
was fantastically

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:14.920
expensive, it was displayed like gold at exhibitions.
Now you

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.650
find it everywhere. For example, you can find
it quite easily

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:22.730
here you have thin foil of aluminium which
is used as the

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:27.000
covering for pill packets. You may easily
have eaten lunch

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.320
today from sandwiches what were wrapped up
in aluminium

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:36.360
foil and it’s used in the laboratories in
all sorts of different

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:43.430
ways. It is a very good reflective material
so chemists and

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:48.510
engineers often put aluminium coatings on
mirrors like this

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:53.760
one. Usually if you have a mirror in your
bathroom the metal

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.850
coating is at the back, so that when you spit
when cleaning

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:02.880
your teeth you don’t damage the mirror but
when you are

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.750
doing experiments particularly with ultra
violet light that is

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:13.260
absorbed by glass, or infra red light as well,
you have this as

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:16.641
a coating on the front of your mirror. So
here you have a

00:01:16.641 --> 00:01:19.670
quite nice example of a front coated aluminium
mirror.

